{%- doc -%}
  Prints "1" when an image may be shown on the storefront, and nothing when
  it may not. Callers capture the output and test it for blank.

  An image is held back when its file name contains one of the markers below.
  Those files must not appear in menus, cards or product galleries; the
  proper fix is to remove them from the product in the admin, and this check
  is the safety net until that is done (and if one is ever added again).

  @param {string} src - the image's src
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign pk_markers = 'NP0,_NP_,NT.Patches,Ninja_,fauxpatchexplainer,Patch_PrintEmb,Kraken' | split: ','
  comment
    Found on 2026-10-02 by comparing the pictures themselves rather than
    their names: files that are the same picture as one on another store, and
    the "features" graphics re-made from that store's. A marker here must match
    only those files, never a photo of our own (the "...detailImagecollage"
    photos are ours, so the three detailImage markers end in the extension).
  endcomment
  assign pk_markers_more = 'detailImage.jpg,detailImage_1.jpg,detailImages.jpg,PatchMOCK,PatchForJacketMOCK,VelcroBackpackMock,JacketVelcroMock,VelcroHatMock,FunnyVelcro2,EMBhat_,EMBbeanie_,hatleather,rubberhat,subhat,ArmyPatch_1,MilitaryPatch,FunnyPatch_1,moralepatch,PolicePatch_2,FootballPatch,GirlScoutPatch,NavyPatch3,FlagPatch2,SportsPatch_1,Chenille_1_No_BG,STICKER_2,Patches_Proof,DALL_E2023,1d5c9780-1876,glow.gif' | split: ','
  assign pk_markers = pk_markers | concat: pk_markers_more
  assign pk_image_ok = '1'
  for pk_marker in pk_markers
    if src contains pk_marker
      assign pk_image_ok = ''
      break
    endif
  endfor
  echo pk_image_ok
-%}
